<title>FRANCE: Alcatel Alsthom H1 net loss 0.4 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Alcatel Alsthom H1 net loss 0.4 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in billions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net					loss  0.4  vs     loss  1.2</p>
<p>    Operating					0.5  vs	     1.4</p>
<p>    Net sales				     74.3  vs	    78.3</p>
<p>    Orders					  81.5  vs	    78.5</p>
<p>    Financial expense			    0.6  vs	     0.2</p>
<p>    Restructuring costs			  0.2  vs	     0.6</p>
<p>    Goodwill amortization			1.1  vs	     1.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax				  loss  1.1  vs     loss  0.1</p>
<p>    Tax					gain  0.1  vs    charge 1.3</p>
<p>    Cashflow					 2.1  vs	     2.5</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity			36.8  vs	    33.0</p>
<p>    Reserves for liabilities/charges	49.9  vs	    50.6</p>
<p>    Net debt					23.0  vs	    20.0</p>
<p>    Gearing					 62    vs	    61</p>
<p>Breakdown of operating income by segment</p>
<p>     - Telecoms			    loss  1.1  vs	loss 0.5</p>
<p>     - Cable			     income  0.9  vs    income 1.1</p>
<p>     - 50 percent of GEC Alsthom   income  0.6  vs    income 0.6</p>
<p>     - Systems			     loss  0.1  vs	loss 0.2</p>
<p>     - Batteries			 income  0.1  vs    income 0.1</p>
<p>     - Other			     income  0.1  vs    income 0.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Alcatel Alsthom said in a statement that its total asset sales since 1995 were 4.9 billion francs and accounted for half of its 10 billion franc 1996 disposal programme.</p>
<p>It said the asset sales would be completed in coming months, resulting in a substantial reduction of the debt to equity ratio.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
